    "created_at": "2019-01-09T22:00:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-09T22:00:32Z",
    "body": "I think *composed tree* as a spec concept is still a useful thing. I do agree that the actual definition should really be done via composed-parent / composed-child relationship instead of some algorithm generating a new tree because composed tree is really just a way of traversing the existing DOM trees interconnected via shadow host/root.",
